Ladybird paints one mask for each CRLF pair in text a script creates.
A lone CR and a lone LF each get a mark. Chrome 158.0.8127.36 also
paints one mark for CRLF in LayoutText::SecureText(). Firefox 151.0
and WebKit 26.5 paint two. Gecko masks each character in
nsCaseTransformTextRunFactory::TransformString(). WebKit masks the
characters of the rendered string in RenderText::secureText().

When pre-line preserves a line feed in unmasked text, Ladybird keeps
the line break even when CR and LF form one grapheme. Two CRLF pairs
produce three lines in all three engines, with ASCII or Latin text.
